
                     #####################################
                     TEST Directory for the Tinker Package
                     #####################################

      This directory contains the source code and reference files for the
      Tinker unit test suite. The tests are built separately from the main
      Tinker executables, and require that the Tinker library has already
      been built in the ../source directory.

      The provided Makefile can be rebuilt after adding, removing or
      changing test source files by running the local "buildmake.py" script
      from within this directory:

          ./buildmake.py *.f > Makefile

      After the Makefile is present, run "make" from this directory to
      compile the unit test executables. Run "make test" to execute the
      base level of the test suite, or "make test LEVEL=5" to execute
      the full suite; the test levels are described below.

      Each test case carries a level, and the levels are ordered by cost.
      A run at level L executes every case at level L or lower:

          1   base       core in-process energy, gradient, virial
          2   analytic   other in-process single-point and unit checks
          3   numerical  finite-difference checks, mostly via
                         testgrad, testlmda and testvir
          4   dynamics   molecular dynamics, sampling and
                         minimization runs
          5   output     program runs compared against reference output

      Select the level with the LEVEL variable, for example "make test
      LEVEL=3". A subset of tests can be selected by passing a name or
      tag with the FILTER variable, for example "make test FILTER=amoeba".
      Without FILTER the default level is 1; with FILTER it is 5, so all
      cases matching the filter are run unless LEVEL is also given. Per-
      check detail lines can be printed by setting DETAIL to "-v", for
      example "make test FILTER=amoeba DETAIL=-v".

      The test binary can also be run directly from this directory with
      the same options:

          ./tinkertest.x [filter] [-l level] [-v]

      The tests use all available OpenMP threads by default, which is
      slow on the small test systems. To run them on a single core, set
      OMP_NUM_THREADS on the command line, which is also inherited by any
      Tinker programs the tests launch:

          OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 make test
          OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 make test LEVEL=5
          OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 make test FILTER=<tag>

